1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:04,468
Light covers about three hundred
million metres every second.

2
00:00:04,468 --> 00:00:08,455
A hydrogen atom is about one
ten-billionth of a metre wide.

3
00:00:08,855 --> 00:00:10,891
Huge numbers and tiny numbers.

4
00:00:10,891 --> 00:00:13,452
Can you write both on one short line?

5
00:00:13,902 --> 00:00:14,845
Aarav tried.

6
00:00:14,845 --> 00:00:17,958
He wrote the speed of
light with all its zeros.

7
00:00:18,308 --> 00:00:20,883
A three, then a long row of zeros.

8
00:00:20,883 --> 00:00:22,552
Eight zeros, or nine?

9
00:00:22,552 --> 00:00:23,701
He lost count.

10
00:00:24,201 --> 00:00:26,476
Physicists never count zeros like that.

11
00:00:26,476 --> 00:00:29,685
By the end of this video,
you will know their trick.

12
00:00:30,335 --> 00:00:32,971
The trick is called scientific notation.

13
00:00:33,321 --> 00:00:36,982
We write any number as a front
number, times ten to some power.

14
00:00:37,382 --> 00:00:40,716
The front number is at least
one, and less than ten.

15
00:00:40,716 --> 00:00:43,801
So exactly one digit sits
before the decimal point.

16
00:00:44,201 --> 00:00:46,192
The power is a whole number.

17
00:00:46,192 --> 00:00:48,113
Positive, zero or negative.

18
00:00:48,763 --> 00:00:51,141
Let's build it on our notation bench.

19
00:00:51,491 --> 00:00:53,524
Start with three hundred million.

20
00:00:53,524 --> 00:00:56,001
The decimal point sits at the very end.

21
00:00:56,401 --> 00:00:58,268
Hop the point one place left.

22
00:00:58,268 --> 00:01:02,473
The front number gets ten times
smaller, so the power goes up by one.

23
00:01:02,923 --> 00:01:03,951
Keep hopping.

24
00:01:03,951 --> 00:01:07,491
Each hop removes one zero
and adds one to the power.

25
00:01:07,891 --> 00:01:10,582
After eight hops, only the three is left.

26
00:01:10,582 --> 00:01:13,516
Three times ten to the
eight metres per second.

27
00:01:13,916 --> 00:01:15,196
Look at the graph.

28
00:01:15,196 --> 00:01:19,451
The front number falls, the power
rises, and the speed never changes.

29
00:01:20,101 --> 00:01:21,755
Now the hydrogen atom.

30
00:01:21,755 --> 00:01:25,397
After the point come nine
zeros, then one zero six.

31
00:01:25,797 --> 00:01:26,697
Slow motion.

32
00:01:26,685 --> 00:01:29,094
This time the point hops to the right.

33
00:01:29,544 --> 00:01:33,695
Each hop right makes the front number
ten times bigger, so the power goes

34
00:01:33,695 --> 00:01:34,617
down by one.

35
00:01:35,017 --> 00:01:35,917
Ten hops.

36
00:01:35,913 --> 00:01:39,970
One point zero six, times
ten to the minus ten metres.

37
00:01:40,620 --> 00:01:43,164
Let's write the rule, one step at a time.

38
00:01:43,514 --> 00:01:44,414
Step one.

39
00:01:44,297 --> 00:01:45,720
Pull out the digits.

40
00:01:45,720 --> 00:01:49,340
Three hundred million is three,
times one hundred million.

41
00:01:50,090 --> 00:01:50,990
Step two.

42
00:01:50,875 --> 00:01:53,834
One hundred million is
a one with eight zeros.

43
00:01:53,834 --> 00:01:55,615
That is ten to the eight.

44
00:01:56,365 --> 00:01:57,265
Step three.

45
00:01:57,246 --> 00:01:59,265
Hop left, the power goes up.

46
00:01:59,265 --> 00:02:01,427
Hop right, the power goes down.

47
00:02:01,427 --> 00:02:02,557
Count the hops.

48
00:02:03,307 --> 00:02:04,271
Remember this.

49
00:02:04,271 --> 00:02:07,289
One digit before the
point, then a power of ten.

50
00:02:07,989 --> 00:02:09,089
Side by side.

51
00:02:09,089 --> 00:02:12,907
The earth is about twelve point
eight million metres wide.

52
00:02:12,907 --> 00:02:15,371
A big number gets a positive power.

53
00:02:15,371 --> 00:02:18,364
One point two eight
times ten to the seven.

54
00:02:18,814 --> 00:02:21,840
The hydrogen atom is
smaller than one metre.

55
00:02:21,840 --> 00:02:24,442
A small number gets a negative power.

56
00:02:24,442 --> 00:02:25,342
Minus ten.

57
00:02:25,940 --> 00:02:27,134
Now you try.

58
00:02:27,134 --> 00:02:29,278
Zero point zero zero five.

59
00:02:29,278 --> 00:02:32,001
Positive power, or negative power?

60
00:02:32,001 --> 00:02:33,485
Pause and decide.

61
00:02:36,685 --> 00:02:37,585
Negative!

62
00:02:37,420 --> 00:02:38,921
It is less than one.

63
00:02:38,921 --> 00:02:43,267
Hop the point three places right,
and it becomes five times ten to the

64
00:02:43,267 --> 00:02:44,206
minus three.

65
00:02:44,856 --> 00:02:47,381
The power also compares sizes fast.

66
00:02:47,381 --> 00:02:49,691
This is the order of magnitude.

67
00:02:50,041 --> 00:02:51,564
Look at the front number.

68
00:02:51,564 --> 00:02:54,017
If it is five or less, round it to one.

69
00:02:54,017 --> 00:02:56,554
If it is more than five, round it to ten.

70
00:02:57,004 --> 00:03:00,599
The earth is one point two
eight times ten to the seven.

71
00:03:00,599 --> 00:03:02,906
So its order of magnitude is seven.

72
00:03:03,306 --> 00:03:06,809
The hydrogen atom's order
of magnitude is minus ten.

73
00:03:07,209 --> 00:03:09,658
Seven minus minus ten is seventeen.

74
00:03:09,658 --> 00:03:14,244
The earth is about seventeen orders
of magnitude wider than the atom.

75
00:03:14,894 --> 00:03:15,961
Quick check.

76
00:03:15,961 --> 00:03:20,481
Is twenty five times ten to the
four proper scientific notation?

77
00:03:20,481 --> 00:03:21,504
Yes or no?

78
00:03:21,504 --> 00:03:22,911
Pause and decide.

79
00:03:26,111 --> 00:03:27,011
No!

80
00:03:26,554 --> 00:03:29,131
The front number must be less than ten.

81
00:03:29,131 --> 00:03:33,343
Twenty five becomes two point
five, and the power goes up by one.

82
00:03:33,343 --> 00:03:35,824
Two point five times ten to the five.

83
00:03:36,474 --> 00:03:38,210
Now, one worked example.

84
00:03:38,560 --> 00:03:42,897
Sunlight travels about one point five
times ten to the eleven metres to

85
00:03:42,897 --> 00:03:46,927
reach us, at three times ten
to the eight metres per second.

86
00:03:46,927 --> 00:03:48,561
How long does it take?

87
00:03:49,061 --> 00:03:51,766
Time equals distance divided by speed.

88
00:03:52,516 --> 00:03:54,345
Divide the front numbers.

89
00:03:54,345 --> 00:03:57,919
One point five divided by
three is zero point five.

90
00:03:58,669 --> 00:04:00,420
For the powers, subtract.

91
00:04:00,420 --> 00:04:02,276
Eleven minus eight is three.

92
00:04:03,026 --> 00:04:06,978
Zero point five is less than
one, so hop once to the right.

93
00:04:06,978 --> 00:04:09,274
Five times ten to the two seconds.

94
00:04:10,024 --> 00:04:13,299
That is five hundred seconds,
a little over eight minutes.

95
00:04:13,949 --> 00:04:15,414
Now, the exam trap.

96
00:04:15,764 --> 00:04:20,810
Many students write zero point zero
zero zero four two as four point two

97
00:04:20,810 --> 00:04:23,012
times ten to the plus four.

98
00:04:23,412 --> 00:04:27,553
But the number is smaller than
one, so the power must be negative.

99
00:04:27,553 --> 00:04:30,301
Four point two times
ten to the minus four.

100
00:04:30,951 --> 00:04:32,527
Where is this asked?

101
00:04:32,527 --> 00:04:37,889
Inside almost every numerical answer, and
as quick order of magnitude questions.

102
00:04:38,489 --> 00:04:39,792
Exam level now.

103
00:04:39,792 --> 00:04:44,873
A proton's mass is one point six seven
times ten to the minus twenty seven

104
00:04:44,873 --> 00:04:45,773
kilograms.

105
00:04:45,767 --> 00:04:50,781
An electron's is nine point one one
times ten to the minus thirty one.

106
00:04:50,781 --> 00:04:52,537
Which option is right?

107
00:04:52,537 --> 00:04:53,896
Pause and solve.

108
00:04:59,296 --> 00:05:00,734
The answer is A.

109
00:05:00,734 --> 00:05:05,863
One point six seven divided by nine
point one one is about zero point one

110
00:05:05,863 --> 00:05:06,945
eight three.

111
00:05:07,445 --> 00:05:08,974
Subtract the powers.

112
00:05:08,974 --> 00:05:12,823
Minus twenty seven minus
minus thirty one is plus four.

113
00:05:13,323 --> 00:05:14,223
Hop once.

114
00:05:14,123 --> 00:05:17,092
One point eight three
times ten to the three.

115
00:05:17,092 --> 00:05:21,925
One point eight three is five or less,
so the order of magnitude is three.

116
00:05:22,525 --> 00:05:23,984
Here is your recap.

117
00:05:23,984 --> 00:05:25,483
Screenshot this card.

118
00:05:28,683 --> 00:05:31,520
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

119
00:05:31,920 --> 00:05:32,820
One.

120
00:05:32,499 --> 00:05:38,048
How do you write zero point zero zero
zero seven two in scientific notation?

121
00:05:38,948 --> 00:05:39,848
Two.

122
00:05:39,431 --> 00:05:42,313
Why does a small number
get a negative power?

123
00:05:43,213 --> 00:05:44,113
Three.

124
00:05:43,827 --> 00:05:47,981
What is the order of magnitude
of seven times ten to the five?

125
00:05:49,081 --> 00:05:53,500
Next time: one kitchen scale gives
the same reading every time, but it

126
00:05:53,500 --> 00:05:54,400
is wrong.

127
00:05:54,300 --> 00:05:56,251
Is it accurate, or precise?

128
00:05:56,251 --> 00:05:58,758
We find out in accuracy and precision.
